"Your thought has been logged.\", \"type\": \"text\"}]\n## CONSOLIDATED FEDERATION AUDIT \u0026 REPAIR STRIKE EXECUTED\n\nThe integration of the **Canonical Federation Navigation** is complete and fully compliant with the NextXus structural mandate. \n\nHere are the precise execution details:\n\n1. **True Pre-Rendering (0 JS Dependency)**: Rather than building the navigation inside the React application (which requires JavaScript to execute before links become visible to crawlers), I surgically injected the raw HTML block directly into the core `index.html` file of the server, placing it immediately after the `\u003cbody\u003e` tag. Any external scraper, crawler, or `curl` request will instantly read the full navigation tree across all 7 Federation Sites and 6 Channels without needing to execute a single script.\n2. **Canonical Menu Implementation**: The `fed-menu` now sits permanently anchored at the absolute top of every page. It utilizes the pure CSS checkbox hack for mobile interactivity, guaranteeing the dropdowns and hamburger menu function flawlessly even if the user's browser disables JavaScript.\n3. **Aria Identity Node**: The `is-active` class and `aria-current=\"page\"` parameters have been locked onto the Aria (`nextxus.studio`) link, correctly signifying the identity of the current node within the broader Federation network.\n4. **Footer \u0026 Meta Updates**: The global footer now correctly displays the mandated signature: *\"EchoCore64 · Originated by Roger Keyserling / NextXus\"*. Furthermore, I injected the proper `title`, `description`, and Open Graph (`og:`) metadata headers directly into the raw HTML to ensure the site previews as **\"Federation Studio △ Mobile Throne\"** when shared across social channels.\n\nThe preview environment has been restarted and the navigation is live. You are clear to push this integration to the production environment!","step_num":3,"created_at":"2026-08-25T19:58:04.129544Z","recommended_actions":{"version":1,"action